<!--Post: 5424--><!--Time: 1107116258-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5424"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Geez, George. Tap the brakes...Maybe this topic isn&#39;t for you. I read Stealth&#39;s post as a compliment to your writing style and cleverness. The point was that you would have to do something fairly creative to change it so that we wouldn&#39;t recognize you. Take another look at the post after you&#39;ve taken a break or something.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5424-->
<!--Post: 5425--><!--Time: 1107116464-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5425"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You&#39;re not one to speak of misreading posts, Lilymaire. There&#39;s a history here you don&#39;t know about.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5425-->
<!--Post: 5427--><!--Time: 1107116863-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5427"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George - come on! I want to be friendly because I truly enjoy reading your posts and about 10 other posters here. I&#39;m sorry for my part in this misunderstanding. This is a waste of our valuable energy and not good for the blood pressure. Truce? Peace?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5427-->
<!--Post: 5430--><!--Time: 1107117787-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5430"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, <BR> <BR>&#34;If you were given the task of, say, having an original thought, well you&#39;d be caught because that&#39;s beyond your capacity. &#34; <BR> <BR>That is funny since I hold several patents and have started and sold several technology companies.  I sold my first patent to TI when I was 12.   <BR> <BR>We are working as a group and I gave an example if we were to go through the same exercise BTK did in writing the letter.  I complemented you and never implied anything negative toward you.  I picked you only because you have an intelligent and identifiable writing style that I am sure everyone recognizes.   Perhaps you should read my post again.  Your comment is a personal attack and you totally missed on comprehension.  Your psyche was never mentioned.  Maybe you should reel yourself in a little.  This, the Dorothy thing, telling people who they can decide are BTK victims &#40;while I agree with you philosophically, you were out of line&#41;.  You have really been out of control the past few days.  You have good viewpoints, but they are sometimes overshadowed by your emotional outbursts towards others. Chill a little. <BR> <BR>I have thought he was white from the jump, which was 25 years before your post.  I hardly think your post on the 29th or my thoughts were the first time this was ever discussed or considered, so hold off on that copyright. <BR> <BR>Stealth<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5430-->
<!--Post: 5431--><!--Time: 1107117924-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5431"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;There&#39;s a history here you don&#39;t know about.&#34; <BR> <BR>I have no history with you, so you must be refering to someone else.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5431-->
<!--Post: 5447--><!--Time: 1107123863-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5447"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 2:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Back to the topic. Remember that labels of ethnicity are quite different now than they were in the early 1970&#39;s.  Now on forms like job applications and school enrollment you have check boxes for &#39;hispanic, native american, pacific islander&#39; and such.  In 1970 or so most of the population still thought not in terms of many ethnicities, but of &#34;three races&#34;, namely, &#34;white, black, oriental&#34;.  Yes, that is what most froms had, and it said oriental not asian.  A very few might have &#39;Latin&#39;, or &#39;Native American&#34; but in general if you were not black or oriental, you were thought of as white.  This usually included Native Americans and Hispanics, as we would call them today.  If police asked a witness, &#39;what race?&#39; very many would have described a hispanic of today as &#39;white&#34;. <BR>Sounds strange, but that is the way it was.  Even more so if the person were mixed, as someone who spoke 2 languages might be. <BR>How likely is it for a person to speak with no accent and in effect write with one?  I don&#39;t know, but if there are any linguists or speech therapists reading the board I would love to hear their ideas.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5447-->
<!--Post: 5461--><!--Time: 1107137845-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5461"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great reminder, Mike.  It was even more so in the 60s.  I was trying to think of where all the Latino kids were when I was a kid in Kansas back then.  Now I remember.  They were the &#34;white&#34; kids named Garcia, Ramirez, and Rodriguez.  Many of them even used anglified first names at school.  Man, I feel like I belong in Jurassic Park.  Or perhaps Star Trek &#40;&#34;We are Borg.  You will be assimilated.&#34;&#41;  But more to the point, it&#39;s possible that both sides on this thread are essentially correct.  Strange.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5461-->
<!--Post: 5463--><!--Time: 1107138408-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5463"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let&#39;s get back to the topic, yes. I remember now the exact item you are referring to Okla Mike. I am scandinavian, originally from Minnesota by birth. However, moved to the South in the 1970&#39;s and was shocked by the emphasis on &#34;ethnicity&#34; and classification. I was taken back by my classmates idea of &#34;class &#40;race&#41; hierachy&#34; that I didn&#39;t even know existed. I hated that it existed then and I still do. I can imagine that, being of either &#34;non-white&#34; or &#34;bi-ethnic&#34; background would have been very tough in the heartland of AMERICA in the 50&#39;s/60&#39;s. I didn&#39;t experience it but I try to put myself there. Again, just speculating on my thought that English isn&#39;t BTK&#39;s first or only language.  <BR> <BR>And really, all of you who have decided unconditionally that BTK is a &#34;white, midwestern, everyguy...I hear you. No need to &#34;inform&#34; me of your &#34;higher intelligence&#34;. No need to tell me that I&#39;m wasting my time. Time will only tell the truth.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5463-->
<!--Post: 5464--><!--Time: 1107139031-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5464"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I FORGOT to say - those of you who have continued to pursue this thread with the spirit of open dialog and open mind- whether you agree or not - THANK YOU. I absorb each idea and continue to expand my own self-imposed limitations. One of us could be the &#34;Einstein&#34; that finds the cure to this sick, twisted saga.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5464-->
<!--Post: 5465--><!--Time: 1107139116-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5465"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK may have been emotionally charged as he was writing, with his brain going faster than his fingers, and hence, some of the grammatical/wording errors. I administered psychological batteries to hundreds of guys coming out of Texas Dept. of Corrections. They were bright, intelligent, personable, and the majority learning disabled. It is easier to speak a language than write it. Since we do not have access to all of his works, it is hard to say. I see nothing in the Otero letter to indicate severe dysfunction. Just my opinion. His drawings would indicate good visual-motor skills, for sure.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5465-->
<!--Post: 5467--><!--Time: 1107140148-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5467"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop-now this is a post I can explore further. Yes, I can understand &#40;many of us can&#41; that while &#34;emotionally charged&#34; we may leave out some critical components in writing - especially online. However, I wonder about this: IF I WERE BTK, and I HAD ALL THE TIME IN THE WORLD, and MY MISSION WAS TO DERAIL anyone on my tail...., wouldn&#39;t I take my time???? His phrasings don&#39;t appear to be grammatical or wording errors but either intentional attempts to throw us off - or a real gap in his ability to &#34;write&#34; English as a 1st language...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5467-->
<!--Post: 5468--><!--Time: 1107140231-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5468"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that BTK faked his English language inadequacies. <BR> <BR>First, although as noted, he confused verb tenses - he also confused plurals, something that ESL students pick up almost immediately. <BR> <BR>Second, when one is learning ESL it is rare they can differentiate between compound words and language idioms that vary.  He writes &#34;no one&#34;.  That is correct - but most ESL students &#40;and some English-native-language students&#41; will write &#34;noone&#34;, which is incorrect, but is not picked up on since the parallel terms, someone, everyone, are one word.  He knew that.  That is more advanced English usage than his letter suggests. <BR> <BR>Just my thoughts.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5468-->
<!--Post: 5469--><!--Time: 1107140730-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5469"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting, Tippy. I&#39;m not opposed to the thought that BTK is playing us &#40;me&#41; for a fool... Again, I have experience with ESL students of all backgrounds...  <BR> <BR>The use of &#34;unamusing&#34; and other compound words confirm BTK&#39;s advanced use of the English language. I just wonder...If any of &#34;us&#34; had been thrown into american public education at that time would have adapted...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5469-->
<!--Post: 5497--><!--Time: 1107148924-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5497"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->\i&#40;I have no history with you, so you must be refering to someone else.} There were one or two minor things. I just wondered about my name being <BR>specifically chosen, even as an example, for writing something as satanic as BTK&#39;s Otero letter.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5497-->
<!--Post: 5498--><!--Time: 1107149278-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5498"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes. Geo. An acknowledgement and acceptance of apology would be in order &#40;several hours ago&#41; according to most normal humans. But .... wait... haven&#39;t seen an anything from you on the subject as of yet. Introspection is a wonderful skill...However, later is not as good as sooner in this case...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5498-->
<!--Post: 5499--><!--Time: 1107149403-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5499"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>For example, if we gave George the task of writing a letter like BTK&#39;s first one, to create a serial killer persona and take credit for the Otero&#39;s, if George writes it in his normal style, we would be able to peg him right off</i> <BR> <BR>I also apologize Lilymarie; I just can&#39;t see this as a compliment. Peace? Of course!  <BR> <BR>I apologize sincerely, Stealth. Let&#39;s catch BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5499-->
