<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5528"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 4:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Now that we have Peace, I have a theory about his language and race also.  <BR>I believe he is a white male and very likely to have what we call today racist tendancies. Back in the times he grew up that was pretty much the norm. I do believe he tried to mask his race by faking his writing in the first batch of letters. But he is a poet, he has mastered the English language. Although he attempts to hide this, his ego about his skill of English still stands out. In my opinion his voice on 911 call is not masked. I cannot hear any other accent that stand out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5528-->
<!--Post: 5556--><!--Time: 1107190878-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5556"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clairevoient<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clairevoient<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 9:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Out of chaos... comes order -- and a group hug. <BR> <BR>B_ _T_ _ _K® is delighted when hot pursuit goes up in flames. <BR> <BR>Yes, the language is a disguise – a character creating device. <BR> <BR>He simultaneously verifies his roll and masks himself. <BR> <BR>“It makes me queasy, but I really think he may have been intentionally xx xxxxxxxxxxxxxxx mimicking the Otero&#39;s.” <BR>		Stealth, Sunday, Jan. 30, 2005 - 11:33am <BR> <BR>	&#34;The Juwes are not the men That Will be Blamed for nothing&#34; <BR>		Jack the Ripper, Sunday, Sept. 30 1888 <BR> <BR>	“I may send you the bloody knif that took it out if you only wate a whil longer” <BR>		Jack the Ripper, Tuesday, Oct. 16, 1888 <BR> <BR>Disguise your syntax.  <BR>Disguise your disorder.  <BR>Disguise your race.  <BR>Disguise your age. <BR>Disguise your fear. <BR> <BR>Emulate.  <BR>Imitate.  <BR>Blend in.  <BR>Disappear. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5556-->
<!--Post: 5621--><!--Time: 1107219966-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5621"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 5:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>In my opinion his voice on 911 call is not masked</i> <BR>Nugzter, I agree completely. The letters indicating Hispanic influence is still compelling, but I can only guess and I do believe BTK to be white. Of course one can mimic a voice more easily than a written language, but I agree BTK knew proper English. Again, &#34;That&#39;s correct&#34; from that phone message was I believe unrehearsed, whereas the first part of the message was mentally scripted. Should that tape still be considered a major clue &#40;in general terms as to locating a specific person&#41;? It&#39;s been a while. Just wondering. Is there a point when the voice clue could become counterproductive?   <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR>The Ghoulston Street graffito can never be proved to have been written by JTR nor can any of the letters.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5621-->
<!--Post: 5930--><!--Time: 1107458063-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5930"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 11:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have taken the first two letters to an certificated ESOL teacher in the wichita school district and asked if the language patterns looked like english was his second language. <BR> <BR>I am supposed to get the answer this afternoon. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5930-->
<!--Post: 6056--><!--Time: 1107499324-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6056"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 10:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter, <BR> <BR>Just curious. By &#34;he has mastered the English language,&#34; do you mean he&#39;s better than average with the language, which is where I place him, or do you mean that you believe BTK has a stunning command of the language - an awe-inspiring level of understanding? <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll tell you how I came up with my &#34;better than average&#34; estimate. The first letter is a model of disinformation in several ways, including a  crafted style which appears to clearly to be the writing of a Hispanic person. BTK&#39;s later word games aren&#39;t impressive and I believe BTK considers himself a Bard in his own mind, but he does have some English language skill. Not exceptional, not talented, but above average. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6056-->
<!--Post: 6107--><!--Time: 1107534734-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6107"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 8:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK Letter analyzed by ESOL &#40;English for Speakers of Other Languages&#41; Teacher <BR> <BR> <BR>Teacher’s impressions: <BR> <BR>1.	The sentence structure and vocabulary in some instances is so sophisticated that it does not appear to have been written by an English as a Second Language &#40;ESL&#41;author. Examples: <BR> <BR>     a.	“Since sex criminals do not change their M.O. or by nature cannot do so, I will not change mine.”  [sentence structure] <BR>     b.	&#34;Those three dude&#40;s&#41; you have in custody are just talking to get publicity for the Otero murders.&#34;[sentence structure] <BR>     c.  &#34;How does one cure himself?&#34; [sentence structure] <BR>     d.  &#34;He has already chosen his next victim or victims.&#34; [sentence structure] <BR>     e.  &#34;His radio was blaring.&#34; [vocabulary: blaring] <BR>     f.  &#34;GUILTILY&#34; [vocabulary] <BR> <BR>2.  BTK&#39;s use of punctuation is consistently correct.  For example the commas in &#34;I can&#39;t stop it so the monster goes on, and hurt me as well as society. &#34; and &#34;The next day after I read the paper, I will know, but it to late.&#34;  <BR> <BR>3.  She pointed out the method BTK used to alter his writing: &#42;&#42;he always removed the terminal letters of a word, and always left a whole word behind.&#42;&#42;  Examples: <BR>     BTK alters words this way:  <BR>	Follow[ing] = Follow <BR>	Dude[s] = Dude <BR>	Tie[d] = tie <BR>	Cover[ed] = cover <BR>	Hand[s] = hand <BR>	stripe[d] = stripe <BR>	turn[ed] = turn <BR>	it[&#39;s] = it <BR>	to[o] = to <BR>     BTK does not alter words this way: <BR>	Ti[ed] = ti <BR> <BR>     She pointed out that a word which cannot have end letters removed and still remain a word is &#42;never&#42; changed, and after alteration the remaining word is &#42;always&#42; spelled correctly. <BR> <BR>4.  The grammatical errors are not consistent.  An ESL writer who has not learned how to use &#34;ed&#34; or &#34;ing&#34; would leave it off consistently.  BTK does not:   <BR>&#34;Ed&#34; is used correctly in &#34;pointed&#34;, &#34;spilled&#34;, &#34;needed&#34;, and &#34;killed&#34;.  <BR> <BR>&#34;Ing&#34; is used correctly four times and wrong once in the same sentence: &#34;It&#40;‘s&#41; a big complicated game my friend of the monster play&#40;s&#41; putting victims number&#40;s&#41; down, follow&#40;ing&#41; them, checking up on them, waiting in the dark, waiting, waiting....  <BR> <BR>BTK uses &#34;ing&#34; correctly in &#34;liking&#34;.  She says it is very unlikely that an ESL writer would know the more complex rule for converting &#34;like&#34; to &#34;liking&#34;, while not knowing the simpler rule for converting &#34;follow&#34; to &#34;following&#34;   <BR> <BR>5.  She marked the Otero letter to show the pattern of alterations. &#40; &#41; shows letters removed, [ ] shows spelling errors or missing words.		 <BR> <BR>&#34;I write this letter to you for the sake of the tax payer as well as your time. Those three dude&#40;s&#41; you have in custody are just talking to get publicity for the Otero murders. They know nothing at all. I did it by myself and [with] no ones help. There has been no talk either. Let&#39;s put this straight....&#34;  <BR>…feet tie&#40;d&#41; to the bed… <BR>… Face cover&#40;ed&#41; with a pillow. … <BR>…cord tie&#40;d&#41; in a clove-hitch. <BR>…Hand&#40;s&#41; tie&#40;d&#41; with blind cord. <BR>…All one legnht [length] <BR>…yellow-brown stripe&#40;d&#41; T-shirt. <BR>Hands tie&#40;d&#41; behind their backs. <BR>Slip knotts [knots] on Joe and Joseph&#40;‘s&#41; neck&#40;s&#41; to hold leg&#40;s&#41; down… <BR>Thermostat turn&#40;ed&#41; down. <BR>&#34;I&#39;m sorry this happen&#40;s&#41; to society. They are the ones who suffer the most. It&#40;&#39;s&#41; hard to control myself. You probably call me &#39;psychotic with sexual perversion hang-up&#40;s&#41;.&#39; When this monster enter&#40;ed&#41; my brain I will never know. But, it&#40;&#39;s&#41; here to stay. How does one cure himself? If you ask for help, that you have killed four people they will laugh or hit the panic button and call the cops. <BR>&#34;I can&#39;t stop it so the monster goes on, and hurt&#40;s&#41; me as well as society. Society can be thankful that there are ways for people like me to relieve myself at time&#40;s&#41; by day dreams [daydreams] of some victims being torture&#40;d&#41; and being mine. It&#40;‘s&#41; a big complicated game my friend of the monster play&#40;s&#41; putting victims number&#40;s&#41; down, follow&#40;ing&#41; them, checking up on them, waiting in the dark, waiting, waiting.... the pressure is great and sometimes he run&#40;s&#41; the game to his liking. Maybe you can stop him. I can&#39;t. He has already chosen his next victim or victims. I don&#39;t [know] who they are yet. The next day after I read the paper, I will know, but it&#40;‘s&#41; to&#40;o&#41; late. Good luck hunting. <BR>&#34;YOURS, TRULY GUILTILY&#34; <BR>&#34;P.S. Since sex criminals do not change their M.O. or by nature cannot do so, I will not change mine. The code words for me will be....Bind them, toture [torture] them, kill them, B.T.K., you see he&#40;‘s&#41; at it again. They will be on the next victim.&#34; <BR> <BR>Her conclusion:  Very unlikely to be the result of ESL issues.  The sophistication in vocabulary, and sentence structure plus the lack of consistent misapplication of grammatical rules does not resemble any ESL writings she has seen.   <BR>The inconsistent use of the alterations &#40;removing terminal letters leaving a whole word: &#34;ways is correct while play&#40;s&#41; is not&#41; does not appear to be an ESL issue either. <BR> <BR>Makes me wish I’d stayed awake in English class. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6107-->
